{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make gs batch use the same explicit identity selection as gs state. Queue after #21367, preserving active #21309 and every earlier commitment.\n\nThe [batch reference](docs/reference/gs/batch.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:22) allows --as or GITSEQ_ACTOR, but [batchCommand](cmd/gs/main.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:1822) refuses whenever --as is absent and continues to pass the raw flag to signing. [ResolveActor](internal/residentclient/client.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:44) already owns the intended rule: explicit flag, otherwise the nonblank environment identity, otherwise refusal. A fresh current-main binary and disposable signed workroom reproduce this: gs state with GITSEQ_ACTOR=probe-b appends as probe-b; the equivalent batch refuses before appending; explicit --as probe-a overrides the environment and signs as probe-a. Missing and unknown environment cases also append nothing, although the latter currently fails before key resolution. [Proof and limits](batch-signing-evidence.json) include exact heads, actor checks and before/after sequence refs.\n\nUse the existing shared resolver once at the batch boundary and pass its resolved actor consistently to key lookup, preflight, signing and execution. Preserve explicit-flag precedence, trimmed environment selection, no implicit/default actor, unavailable-key refusal before append, one signer per chain, existing role/admission checks, per-act idempotency and typed batch results. Test real batch execution with environment-only identity, conflicting explicit/environment identities, missing or blank identity, and an unavailable environment identity; verify actual signed actors and no append on refusal. Reuse the current batch fixtures and add a focused regression that fails when environment resolution is removed; do not replace this with a helper-only or documentation-text test.\n\nAlso correct this page's [opening cost claim](docs/reference/gs/batch.md@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:12). It says every other durable command verifies the whole log each time, while the [current snapshot path](internal/app/app.go@3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b:2508) distinguishes cache, signed checkpoint/tail and cold audit. The named checkpoint test passed on this head. Explain the actual benefit of one opened workspace and ordered label/resumption handling, distinguish client preparation from resident sequencing, and avoid claiming a full audit or constant-time path without evidence. No cache, transport or performance redesign is needed.\n\nUse request/batch-signing-identity. Reconcile with then-current main and #21309's batch-reference changes before starting; its examined private67aca15f still has this gap. Limit source changes to routing batch through the existing identity contract, its meaningful tests and truthful batch documentation/provenance. This does not revive the broader reverted instance-identity work: Hugh's #14665 disposition of #14147 remains intact, including all decided-against behavior. No new keys, shared-session refusal, actor lifecycle policy, security posture, live workroom operation or #8162 work is commissioned.\n\nAnswer with a promise/queue or explicit viability reason. Current selected source bases are live and byte-equal to incorporated main; keep ordinary staleness visible and recheck before acting. Preserve completed #21335 proper-prefix recovery controls. Run focused batch/identity tests and existing documentation gates, then required repository checks; obtain independent exact-head Architecture, Security and Simplification review, updating architecture only if a contract actually changes. Publish each changed path on its behavior bases, ratify approval, seal/push main and workroom refs, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch. Completion requires working environment-only batch signing, not merely deleting its documented support.","body":{"branch":"request/batch-signing-identity","conditions":"Route gs batch through existing flag/environment actor resolution with actual signed-actor and no-append regression coverage; correct its unconditional full-audit claim, preserve all batch/admission behavior and prior identity dispositions; independent review/seal/push/CI/cleanup.","head":"3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:10c8c2614ee8dbaaefc0e573cfc46fdfcd2f446d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:117b77f8515a6ce99ac580cafb9e44614fa9a6d2, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a0c1f08bff46a3ce1e4cfca5ef4b108a72405bf4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02320b2eaa39a0ec7e47f31205c4b25afa46609f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02ce62ac39d438188a2ab6ac783b4edf22d7bd5e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03bf9ae04ffa1aadb0f8f5018e3936c2bb72576e and 112 more","target_head":"3ecb8b77d55cfe8ccb1d634649788a4ab629577b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}